#: InstUninstSettingsWidgetData.cpp:48 rc.cpp:63
msgid ""
"Some TrueType fonts have incorrect Postscript names for certain characters.\n"
"\n"
"For example, \"Euro\" is sometimes listed as \"uni20ac\". This would affect "
"any Postscript output from applications (and most produce Postscript when "
"printing), as it would list the use of the \"Euro\" character -but when this "
"Postscript output is sent to the printer, or viewed, the \"Euro\" symbol "
"would not be found.\n"
"\n"
"Selecting this option will cause the installer to automatically correct any "
"broken fonts."
msgstr ""
"Some TrueType fonts have incorrect Postscript names for certain characters.\n"
"\n"
"For example, \"Euro\" is sometimes listed as \"uni20ac\". This would affect "
"any Postscript output from applications (and most produce Postscript when "
"printing), as it would list the use of the \"Euro\" character -but when this "
"Postscript output is sent to the printer, or viewed, the \"Euro\" symbol "
"would not be found.\n"
"\n"
"Selecting this option will cause the installer to automatically correct any "
"broken fonts."

